(25,25,1,'Contract agreement: infrastructure works (proforma)','<h2 style=\"text-align:center\">CONTRACT AGREEMENT<br><span style=\"font-size:12pt\">Infrastructure Works</span></h2><p style=\"font-size:9pt;border:1px solid #999;padding:6px\"><i>Company proforma. Where the ENTITY\'s bidding documents prescribe a contract form or general and special conditions of contract, those govern; this proforma is used only as the ENTITY accepts it. Review with counsel before signing.</i></p><p>This Agreement is made on {{project.contract_date}} at {{entity.city}}, {{entity.province}}, by and between:</p><p><b>{{entity.name}}</b>, a government entity with office at {{entity.address}}, represented by <b>{{entity.head_name}}</b>, {{entity.head_position}} (the \"ENTITY\"); and</p><p><b>{{company.name}}</b>, {{company.reg_no}}, with business address at {{company.address}}, TIN {{company.tin}}, represented by <b>{{signatory.name}}</b>, {{signatory.position}} (the \"SUPPLIER\");</p><p><b>WHEREAS</b>, the ENTITY procured <b>{{project.title}}</b> ({{project.reference_no}}) through {{project.mode}} under {{project.regime}}, funded by {{project.funding_source}};</p><p><b>WHEREAS</b>, the ENTITY awarded the contract to the SUPPLIER by Notice of Award {{project.noa_ref}} dated {{project.noa_date}};</p><p><b>NOW, THEREFORE</b>, the parties agree as follows:</p><p><b>1. Contract documents.</b> The following form part of this Agreement and are read together, in this order of precedence: this Agreement; the Notice of Award; the purchase order or notice to proceed; the bid / quotation of the SUPPLIER with its price schedule; the technical specifications or terms of reference; and the general and special conditions issued by the ENTITY, if any.</p><p><b>2. Scope.</b> The SUPPLIER shall carry out and complete the works as listed below:</p>{{lines.contract_table}}<p><b>3. Contract price.</b> The contract price is <b>{{project.contract_amount}}</b> ({{project.contract_amount_words}}), inclusive of all applicable taxes, duties, delivery and other charges. The ENTITY shall withhold the taxes required by law and issue BIR Form 2307 for them.</p><p><b>4. Period and place.</b> The works at {{project.delivery_site}} shall start upon the notice to proceed dated {{project.ntp_date}} and be completed within {{project.delivery_days}}, on or before {{project.due_date}}. Progress billings follow the accomplishment certified by the ENTITY\'s engineer.</p><p><b>5. Inspection and acceptance.</b> The ENTITY, through its inspection and acceptance committee, shall inspect the deliveries or work and issue its inspection and acceptance report. Items rejected shall be replaced or corrected by the SUPPLIER at its cost within the period the ENTITY sets.</p><p><b>6. Payment.</b> {{project.payment_terms}}. Each billing shall be supported by the sales invoice, statement of account, signed delivery receipts or accomplishment reports and the inspection and acceptance report. A retention of {{project.retention_pct}} of each payment, where applicable, shall be released after the warranty period upon the ENTITY\'s final acceptance.</p><p><b>7. Warranty.</b> The SUPPLIER warrants the goods / work against defects for {{project.warranty_months}} from acceptance and shall correct any defect reported within that period at its cost.</p><p><b>8. Liquidated damages.</b> For each day of delay beyond the agreed period not caused by the ENTITY or by force majeure, the SUPPLIER shall pay liquidated damages of {{project.ld_rate}} of the cost of the unperformed portion, deductible from any amount due.</p><p><b>9. License, securities and insurance.</b> The CONTRACTOR (the SUPPLIER) holds a valid PCAB license for the category and size of this project, posts the performance security required by the contract documents, and keeps the works and its workers insured as the contract documents require. It is liable for defects of the works as provided by law.</p><p><b>10. Changes.</b> No change in quantity, scope, price or period is valid unless approved in writing by the ENTITY\'s authorized official in accordance with the applicable procurement rules.</p><p><b>11. Termination.</b> Either party may terminate this Agreement on the grounds and through the procedures provided by the applicable procurement law, its implementing rules and the contract documents.</p><p><b>12. Governing law and venue.</b> This Agreement is governed by the laws of the Philippines. Disputes shall first be settled amicably; failing that, through the dispute resolution provided by the applicable procurement rules, and the courts of the place of the ENTITY.</p><p><b>13. Entire agreement.</b> This Agreement and the contract documents contain the whole agreement of the parties; amendments are valid only in writing and signed by both.</p><p>IN WITNESS WHEREOF, the parties have signed this Agreement on the date and at the place first written above.</p><table class=\"sig-table\" style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:26px\"><tr><td style=\"width:50%;vertical-align:top;padding:28px 10px 0 0\"><div style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000;min-height:22px\">{{entity.head_name}}</div><div>For the ENTITY: {{entity.head_position}}</div></td><td style=\"width:50%;vertical-align:top;padding:28px 10px 0 0\"><div style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000;min-height:22px\">{{signatory.name}}</div><div>For the SUPPLIER: {{signatory.position}}</div></td></tr></table><p style=\"margin-top:14px\">Signed in the presence of:</p><table class=\"sig-table\" style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:26px\"><tr><td style=\"width:50%;vertical-align:top;padding:28px 10px 0 0\"><div style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000;min-height:22px\"> </div><div>Witness</div></td><td style=\"width:50%;vertical-align:top;padding:28px 10px 0 0\"><div style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000;min-height:22px\"> </div><div>Witness</div></td></tr></table><h3 style=\"margin-top:20px\">ACKNOWLEDGMENT</h3><p>Republic of the Philippines )<